@startuml cursor-lease-state
' The cursor/lease finite-state machine exactly as src/ffi/index.rs enforces
' it: Idle alternates with Leased under next_batch/release_batch, reduce
' leases and auto-releases per callback, End is sticky, and destruction is
' refused while a lease is live. Guards are typeset as LaTeX.
' Color: unleased cursor states = liblevenshtein #FADBD8; the leased state =
'   leased memory #FFECB3 (#FF6F00); terminal Closed = concurrency slate
'   #CFD8DC (#455A64); refusal self-loops annotated with their status names.
' Source of truth: src/ffi/index.rs (fill_batch, next_batch, release_batch,
'   reduce, free); wave-W3 TLA home LlevBatchLease.tla (LLEV-LEASE-1..7);
'   anchor tests tests/ffi_resource_snapshot_semantics.rs.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
  BackgroundColor #FADBD8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

title Cursor lease FSM — Idle ⇄ Leased, sticky End, free refused under a live lease

state "Idle\n(no live lease)" as Idle #FADBD8
state "Leased(g)\nviews + arenas borrowed" as Leased #FFECB3
state "Ended\n(stream exhausted)" as Ended #FADBD8
state "Closed" as Closed #CFD8DC

[*] --> Idle : query start captures\nthe snapshot

Idle --> Leased : next_batch(m) → OK\n<latex>m \ge 1,\; \text{matches remain},\; g := \max(g{+}1 \bmod 2^{64},\, 1)</latex>
Idle --> Ended : next_batch(m) → END\n<latex>m \ge 1,\; \text{no matches remain}</latex>
Idle --> Idle : next_batch(0) →\nINVALID_ARGUMENT
Idle --> Idle : release_batch(g′) →\nINVALID_ARGUMENT «no live lease»
Idle --> Ended : reduce(b, f, ctx) → OK\n«per batch: lease, call f,\nauto-release; f may stop with End»
Idle --> Idle : reduce aborted → f's status\nverbatim «lease released;\ncursor stays usable»

Leased --> Idle : release_batch(g′) → OK\n<latex>g' = g</latex>
Leased --> Leased : release_batch(g′) →\nINVALID_ARGUMENT\n<latex>g' \ne g</latex> «stale or zero»
Leased --> Leased : next_batch / reduce →\nBATCH_IN_USE
Leased --> Leased : free →\nBATCH_IN_USE «not freed;\nownership stays with the caller»

Ended --> Ended : next_batch → END
Idle --> Closed : free → OK
Ended --> Closed : free → OK
Closed --> [*]

note bottom of Leased #FFF8E1
  While leased, the library neither mutates nor
  reallocates the descriptor array or the term
  arenas (UNSAFE_ABI_CONTRACTS.tsv row
  ffi-leased-batch-aliasing); generations are
  strictly increasing and never zero.
end note
@enduml
